g malapropism  are there where in a struggle to make it  make sense they supposed what i was  saying and just missed it completely and  often it's very humorous  these kinds of things so our illusion of  communication is simply that if i were  to read to you a little paragraph from  malaresha to temper do or any work of  depth  we could then spend the rest of the  morning talking about what does the  author mean  you know the ambiguity of of text but if  we were to have a piece of sculpture  in front of us  we  are much more  tightly focused in the same dimension we  who observe it you don't see a different  piece of sculpture than i do i mean to  some degree but not much where in  confrontation with text i may understand  a piece of text perfectly and the  content of it may change my life and  when i ask you what it means you say  well i don't know it's some kind of  verbage this guy couldn't parse a  sentence i couldn't make anything out of  it it just  needs to get a life  so i think that  it's amazing that our global  civilization  is knitted together by nothing more than  small mouth noises  small mouth noises delivered at about 50  hertz  you know 50 cycles per second  and our machines which are now our  prosthesis and which are knitting our  world here they operate at 400 megahertz  and up  uh  literally two orders of magnitude faster  the information is being transferred and  it can be digitalized it can be visual  so  and there's even physiological evidence  for this  for example well i talked about  ayahuasca and how you see sound under  the influence of ayahuasca well  ayahuasca runs on harmolin and dmt  dmt occurs in the brain the human brain  under ordinary metabolic circumstances  and harmine  it turns out occurs in this most  mysterious of all brain  neighborhoods the pineal gland  in the pineal gland is a compound called  a denero adeniroglomerotropine  but when you deconstruct it as a  physical chemist you discover its  5-methoxy no 6-methoxy  tetra